---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../config.mjs';
---
<Base title="How we check answers" description={`How ${SITE_NAME} finds, checks and corrects its chapter numbers.`}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>How we check answers</h1>
    <p class="lede">Every answer is a chapter number with its sources. We keep it that way on purpose.</p>

    <h2>Our rules</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Numbers, not plot.</strong> Answer cards show chapters, volumes and episode numbers. No summaries, character names or arc names beyond a season's official title.</li>
      <li><strong>No cover art.</strong> Later volume covers often reveal new characters, so we don't show them.</li>
      <li><strong>Two sources to agree.</strong> An answer is marked "sources agree" only when two independent pages give the same number. Answers with one source say so.</li>
      <li><strong>Say where it cuts off.</strong> When an episode ends partway through a chapter, the card tells you, and suggests where to start.</li>
      <li><strong>Official releases only.</strong> We link publishers and official apps, never unofficial scan sites.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What the dots mean</h2>
    <ul class="legend">
      <li><span class="dot agree"></span>Two or more sources give the same answer.</li>
      <li><span class="dot differ"></span>Sources disagree by a chapter or so. The card explains the safest place to start.</li>
      <li><span class="dot single"></span>One source so far. If you've read it, you can confirm or correct it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Fixing mistakes</h2>
    <p>Every card has a "This is wrong" link. It opens a short form; we check it against the chapter and update the page, usually within a few days.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 62ch; padding-top: 16px; }
  .prose h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 2.8rem); }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 36px 0 10px; }
  .prose p, .prose li { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .prose ol, .prose ul { padding-left: 22px; }
  .lede { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .legend { list-style: none; padding-left: 0 !important; }
  .dot { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 10px; }
  .dot.agree { background: #1F9D55; }
  .dot.differ { background: #D99A00; }
  .dot.single { border: 2px solid var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
